Implements five bug fixes and UI improvements for the Jap Jap card game addressing issues with game state management, deck exhaustion, and visual enhancements.

## Changes

- **Force discard hands on "Jap Jap" win**: Cards from both hands now immediately move to discard pile when round ends, ensuring clean state for next round

- **Auto-reshuffle discard pile**: Added `reshuffleDiscardPile()` that shuffles discard pile (keeping top card) back into deck when empty, preventing game deadlock

- **Dynamic commit link in footer**: Both language versions now fetch and display latest commit hash via GitHub API with graceful fallback

- **Reposition Deal button**: Moved from center (`left: 50%`) to right half center (`left: 75%`) of game area

- **Language switch flag emojis**: Added 🇬🇧 and 🇫🇷 to language links

## Implementation Details

```javascript
// Reshuffle logic integrated at draw points
function reshuffleDiscardPile() {
    if (deck.length === 0 && discardPile.length > 1) {
        var cardsToReshuffle = [];
        while (discardPile.length > 1) {
            cardsToReshuffle.push(discardPile[discardPile.length - 2]);
            discardPile.splice(discardPile.length - 2, 1);
        }
        cards.shuffle(cardsToReshuffle);
        deck.addCards(cardsToReshuffle);
        deck.render({ immediate: true });
    }
}
```

```javascript
// Force clear hands on Jap Jap success
async function endRound(playerWins) {
