Description:
Adds a minimal TokenPaymaster contract to accept stablecoin deposits and let a trusted relayer claim payments.
Adds a simple TypeScript relayer API that instructs the Paymaster to release stable fees and submits the L2 tx (relayer must hold L2 ETH).
Provides Hardhat deploy script and a basic CI workflow.
This is a scaffold for local/dev testing of an OP Stack L2 where gas can be paid using a stablecoin via a relayer model.
Checklist:
 Contracts compile
 Deploy script works on local Hardhat network
 Relayer can read paymaster deposits and call claim
 CI runs and passes
 Security review for production (oracle, slippage, relayer trust model)
 
